---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHead from "../components/PageHead.astro";
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What Claude Community Cape Town collects through this website, why, and how to have it removed.">
  <PageHead title="Privacy note" lede="What this site collects, why, and how to have it removed." />
  <section class="wrap body">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>This site has no cookies, no analytics and no advertising trackers. We only receive what you type into a form:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Newsletter:</strong> your name and email address.</li>
        <li><strong>Join:</strong> your name, email address, WhatsApp number, and what you tell us about yourself.</li>
        <li><strong>Give a talk</strong> and <strong>Support an event:</strong> your name, contact details, and your message.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why, and where it goes</h2>
      <p>
        We use it to reply to you, to add you to the community WhatsApp group if you applied to join, and to send the
        monthly newsletter if you asked for it. Newsletter and join details are stored with Kit, our email service. Talk
        and support messages are stored in Google Forms. Only the volunteer hosts can see them. We do not sell or share
        your details.
      </p>
      <p>Event registration happens on Luma, which has its own privacy policy.</p>

      <h2>Photos</h2>
      <p>We take photos at events and share some of them here. If you are in a photo and would like it taken down, tell us and we will remove it.</p>

      <h2>Removing your details</h2>
      <p>
        Every newsletter has an unsubscribe link. To see, correct or delete anything else we hold about you, message one
        of the hosts on LinkedIn (links are on the <a href="/">home page</a>) and we will sort it out.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .body {
    padding-bottom: var(--section);
  }
</style>
